Audio observation for libpeer (extern/libpeer): classify every inbound
RTP packet and log the classification, so "does the cloud send audio at
all?" stops being a guess.

extern/libpeer is a git SUBMODULE, so its sources must not be edited in
place: the next `git submodule update` would throw the changes away.  This
patch is applied to the checked out tree by
tools/apply-libpeer-switch-patches.sh, right before libpeer is built (it is
the twelfth patch of that series, after 0001-switch-webrtc-fixes,
0002-no-stdout-log, 0003-h265-depacketizer, 0004-dtls-diagnostics,
0005-ice-roles-prflx-and-timing, 0006-dtls-fingerprint-and-verify,
0007-ice-timeout-and-verify-none, 0008-dtls-bio-remb-and-candidate-dedup,
0009-sctp-init-and-diagnostics, 0010-hole-attribution and
0011-pli-trigger).

Why
---

The 2026-10-24 capture: our session receives video and 2653 decoded
frames, but ZERO audio tracks and ZERO audio packets -- while the official
web client on the same account receives ~40 audio packets per second.
The breakpoint has narrowed to "the cloud does not send audio packets"
vs "we drop them", and NOTHING on the libpeer side could tell those
apart:

  * rtp_decode_generic() (src/rtp.c) has no packet counters at all --
    only the H.264 path counts anything;
  * the receive path classifies packets (audio SSRC / video SSRC / PT
    sniffing) but only counts the classes it likes -- a packet that
    matched NEITHER stream was dropped silently.

What
---

  * Four counters on PeerConnection, bumped exactly where the streams
    are told apart (the is_audio_payload + SSRC site that already
    exists -- no separate payload-type table is introduced):

      rtp_packets_total      audio + video + unmatched
      rtp_audio_packets      matched the audio stream (SSRC or audio PT;
                             PT 63 = RED counts as audio, like the site
                             always did)
      rtp_video_packets      matched the video stream
      rtp_unmatched_packets  matched NEITHER (the old silent drop)

    plus rtp_learned_audio_ssrc: the SSRC the PT-sniffing learned, set
    at the moment it learns (kept distinct from remote_assrc, which may
    also come from the SDP; 0 = the sniffing never fired).

  * One diagnostic line every 5 s (PEER_RTP_CLASS_DIAG_INTERVAL_MS):

      udp_class=rtp audio=%u video=%u unmatched=%u total=%u audioSsrc=%u

    Time-based on purpose: the line must keep printing when there is
    nothing to report.  The engine-side whitelist (patch 0035) needs the
    key "udp_class=rtp" for this line to reach nxjs-debug.log; the
    learning moment already logs "learned_audio_ssrc=... pt=..."
    (key "learned_audio_ssrc").

  * RED (RFC 2198) is NOT unwrapped here, deliberately.  The question
    this patch answers is "do audio packets arrive at all"; PT 63 is
    classified as audio either way, and the unwrapping already exists on
    the app side (apps/audioprobe/opus-format.js, with tests) for the
    day the answer is "yes" and the payload itself matters.

  * Task B extension: the chain AFTER arrival, one step deeper.  The
    classification above says a packet matched the audio stream; it says
    nothing about whether anything came out of it.  rtp_decode_generic()
    (src/rtp.c) kept no books at all, so "arrived but not depacketized"
    and "depacketized but not consumed" were indistinguishable.  It now
    counts, on RtpDecoder (the audio instance is artp_decoder):

      audio_packets_parsed   rtp_parse_payload() accepted the packet;
      audio_units_produced   the audio callback really fired;
      audio_fail_short       parse failed: shorter than an RTP header;
      audio_fail_shape       parse failed: the CSRC / extension /
                             padding / version family;
      audio_red_packets      parse OK and PT 63 (RED) -- now visibly
                             "not unwrapped here" instead of silent;
      audio_opus_packets     parse OK and PT 111 (OPUS).

    A second line rides the same prefix (no new whitelist key):

      udp_class=rtp audioChain recv=.. parsed=.. produced=..
                           failShort=.. failShape=.. redPt=.. opusPt=..

    Honest layer boundary: "opus parameters wrong" is NOT observable
    here (libpeer does not parse opus) -- that verdict belongs to the
    engine's decoder error line one layer up.

How the criterion changes (AGENTS.md 6.2, rule 8)
---------------------------------------------------

  * fault present (no audio sent): audio=0 while total (and video) grow;
  * audio sent but dropped by us: audio>0 with no sound in the app --
    the search moves to OUR decode path;
  * unexpected stream: unmatched>0 -- the cloud sending on an SSRC we
    never negotiated;
  * task B, arrived-but-not-depacketized: recv > parsed on the
    audioChain line (failShort / failShape say which shape is wrong);
  * task B, depacketized-but-not-consumed: parsed > produced (no audio
    callback registered);
  * task B, RED-only sender: redPt > 0 with opusPt == 0 -- the payload
    needs RFC 2198 unwrapping that nobody does on this side.

Every one of them moves, so the line is a criterion and not a
decoration.

A host-side self test of the rule itself is next to this file:
tools/libpeer-switch/0012-audio-observation-check.mjs

Note for the Switch build
-------------------------

struct PeerConnection is PRIVATE to src/peer_connection.c (it is not in
an installed header), so appending fields moves no ABI: the engine never
allocates it by layout.  struct RtpDecoder DOES live in the installed
src/rtp.h and gains six fields at its END (after pli_last_sent_ms) --
same rule as 0011: libpeer.a has to be rebuilt and the installed headers
refreshed together with the engine, otherwise the engine and libpeer
disagree about the struct layout (silent memory corruption, not a clean
compile error).

